+### Auto-Update Deployment
+
+The gateway supports automatic updates when running in Docker. When new commits are pushed to the repository, the container can automatically pull changes, rebuild, and restart with zero downtime.
+
+#### Quick Start
+
+```bash
+# Using HTTPS with GitHub token
+docker-compose -f docker/autoupdate/examples/docker-compose.https.yml up -d
+
+# Using SSH with deploy key
+docker-compose -f docker/autoupdate/examples/docker-compose.ssh.yml up -d
+```
+
+#### Features
+
+- **Automatic polling**: Checks for updates at configurable intervals
+- **Zero-downtime updates**: Atomic build swaps with health verification
+- **Manual trigger**: Update on-demand via `scripts/autoupdate-check.sh`
+- **Rollback support**: Automatic rollback on failed updates
+- **Dual auth support**: GitHub HTTPS token or SSH deploy key
+
+#### Configuration
+
+| Variable | Required | Default | Description |
+|----------|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `UPDATE_INTERVAL` | No | `300` | Check interval in seconds |
+| `GIT_REPO_URL` | Yes | - | Repository URL |
+| `GIT_AUTH_TOKEN` | HTTPS | - | GitHub personal access token |
+| `SSH_PRIVATE_KEY` | SSH | - | SSH deploy key (base64 encoded) |
+| `HEALTH_CHECK_URL` | No | `http://localhost:8080/health` | Health endpoint |
+| `MAX_RETRIES` | No | `3` | Retry attempts for transient failures |
+
+#### Manual Update Trigger
+
+```bash
+# Trigger update check from host
+scripts/autoupdate-check.sh <container_name>
+
+# Or send SIGUSR1 directly
+docker exec <container_name> pkill -SIGUSR1 entrypoint.sh
+```
+
+#### Testing
+
+```bash
+# Run integration tests
+scripts/test-autoupdate.sh
+```
+
+See [docker/autoupdate/README.md](docker/autoupdate/README.md) for detailed documentation.
+
